Display all declared agent preview features, including disabled features,
sorted by name. Each entry includes its name, description, and On or Off status,
matching the default format of 'azd config list-alpha'.

Status uses the same opt-in checks as agent operations: per-feature user config,
the process environment, the selected azd environment (-e), and every azure.yaml
service's env mapping. Any enabling source turns a feature on; false does not
override another source's opt-in.
Only alpha.<ID> config keys apply; alpha.all does not enable agent previews.

Without a project or default environment, the available sources still apply.
An invalid explicit environment or a source read error fails without printing
feature records. This command is always available and needs no preview opt-in.

Usage
  azd ai agent list-alpha [flags]

Global Flags
  -C, --cwd string         : Sets the current working directory
      --debug              : Enables debug and diagnostics logging
  -e, --environment string : The name of the environment to use
  -h, --help               : help for list-alpha
      --no-prompt          : Runs without prompts. Uses existing values; fails if any required value or decision cannot be resolved automatically.
  -o, --output string      : The output format (supported: default) (default "default")

Examples
  List every agent preview feature and its effective status
    azd ai agent list-alpha

  Read values from a specific environment
    azd ai agent list-alpha --environment dev

  Enable voice through user config
    azd config set alpha.agents.voice on

  Alternatively, enable voice in the selected environment
    azd env set AZD_FOUNDRY_EXT_ENABLE_AGENTS_VOICE true
